     3,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><div><blockquote type=\"cite\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><br>Hi all,<br><br>I would like to generate a random negative binomial \r\nsample at each MCMC iteration, which is easy enough with \r\nneg_binomial_rng. The issue is that in my model I run:<br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code>increment_log_prob<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">((</span>neg_binomial_log<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Exposure</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span>n<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">],(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Mu</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span>n<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]*</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]),</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">])-</span>neg_binomial_cdf_log<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">MaxExposure</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Mu</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">,</span>n<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]*</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]),</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">])));</span></code></div>to implement a truncated density. Anything greater than MaxExposure is <i>a priori</i> impossible.<br><br>So\r\n when I generate a random number, I want it to be from the truncated \r\ndensity. The T[,] operation doesn&#39;t work in the generated quantities \r\nblock, so I wrote a little hack to resample anything that exceeds \r\nMaxExposure:<br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code>vector<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span>N<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span> scrapExposure<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br>vector<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span>N<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span> scrap<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br>real <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">int</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Ticker</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br><br><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">########################################################################### RNG</span><br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span> n <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span>N<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><br>      <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Ticker</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br>      <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">while</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Ticker</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">==</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">)</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span>neg_binomial_rng<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">((</span>exp<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Theta</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">])*</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]),</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]);</span><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">if</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">MaxExposure</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Ticker</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">0</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;}</span><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">else</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Ticker</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;}}</span><br><br>       scrapExposure<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span>n<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br>       <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span></code></div><br>But I&#39;m not sure if it should instead be something like this:<br><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code>vector<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span>N<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span> scrapExposure<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br>vector<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span>N<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">2</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]</span> scrap<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br>real <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">int</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Ticker</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><br><br><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">########################################################################### RNG</span><br>  <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">for</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span> n <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">in</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span>N<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><span></span><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span> <span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;-</span>neg_binomial_rng<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">((</span>exp<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Theta</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">])*</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]),</span>B<span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,102,102)\">1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]);</span><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">if</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">(</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">&lt;=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">MaxExposure</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">){</span><br>        <code><code><span>scrapExposure</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span>n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Nscrap</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span>}</span></code></code><br>        <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,136)\">else</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">{</span><br>       <span>scrapExposure</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">[</span><span>n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">]&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\"></span><code><code><code><code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\"><code><code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">MaxExposure</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"></span></code></code></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">;</span><span>}</span></code></code><span><br></span></code></code><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">}</span><br>    <br><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\"></span></code></div>where anything over the truncation point gets rounded down to the maximum.<br><br>I\r\n think the first version is right but any feedback would be appreciated.\r\n Especially if there is already some code on how to do this.<br><br><br>On\r\n a more fun note, I had a dream the other night where a private jet, a \r\nfighter jet escort, and a FedEx truck flew over my city... followed by \r\ntons of SWAT vehicles on the ground. Luckily, I was able to get to where\r\n they were all going---an unveiling of the next generation Google Glass.\r\n I pushed my way to the front, and saw the Google exec finish a demo on \r\nemail using GoogleGlass, only to see Andrew Gelman take the glasses and say &quot;If you think \r\nemail on your glasses is cool, I can fit a mixed effects model on \r\npeoples shoes color predicting political affiliation, and run it in Stan\r\n right on my glasses&quot; He then proceeded to tap the air in front of his \r\nglasses while looking at the crowd, to mark indicator variables that \r\nGoogleStan could automatically compile into a model. Before he finished \r\nhe remarked it was stupid to fit a model of shoe color and political \r\naffiliation, and then left. The future looks bright!</div><div><br></div></blockquote></div></div></div></div>"
